<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The one colour Android itself needs to know about.

    Everything else in this app is a design token in lib/design/tokens.dart, and
    CLAUDE.md rule 8 says a hex code inside a widget is a bug. The launch window
    is the exception that proves it: it is painted by the operating system
    before a single line of Dart has run, so there is no token layer available
    to ask. Keep it in step with `LamplightColors.dark.canvas`.

    It is the DARK canvas in both system themes, deliberately, because the app
    itself defaults to dark whatever the phone is set to. Getting this wrong the
    obvious way — leaving the template's white — means a full-screen white flash
    before a near-black app, in an app people open in the evening. One dark
    frame for someone who has chosen light mode is much the smaller cost.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="lamplight_canvas">#0F0F0E</color>
</resources>
